      { "@type": "Question", "name": "What is a Banjara gotra, and why does it matter?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "A gotra is a patrilineal clan identifier, inherited from your father. In Banjara tradition, marriage within your own gotra is considered forbidden (gotra exogamy), so confirming gotra compatibility is one of the first steps in any match. See our full Banjara Gotra List for details." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Can two people from the same gotra marry?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "No. Same-gotra marriage is not permitted under traditional Banjara custom, since people sharing a gotra are considered to share ancestry. This rule is enforced strongly across most Banjara sub-communities and tanda panchayats." } },
